    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Definition\n\nModulus of Rigidity (G) - also known as Shear Modulus - is the coefficient of elasticity for a shearing force.\n\n**Shear Modulus** = Shear Stress / Shear Strain\n\n### Key Information\n\n- Modulus of Rigidity can be experimentally determined from the slope of a stress-strain curve created during tensile tests conducted on a sample of the material.\n- 1 GPa = 10⁹ Pa = 0.145×10⁶ psi (lbf/in²)\n- 1×10⁶ psi = 6.9 GPa"
